{"pull": {"id": "number:19865", "number": 19865, "title": "KAFKA-18376: High CPU load when AsyncKafkaConsumer uses a small max poll value", "state": "closed", "draft": true, "created_at": "2025-05-30T17:26:03Z", "closed_at": "2025-06-03T14:22:21Z", "merged_at": null, "user": {"login": "kirktrue", "id": 92057, "node_id": "MDQ6VXNlcjkyMDU3", "avatar_url": "https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/92057?v=4", "gravatar_id": "", "url": "https://api.github.com/users/kirktrue", "html_url": "https://github.com/kirktrue", "followers_url": "https://api.github.com/users/kirktrue/followers", "following_url": "https://api.github.com/users/kirktrue/following{/other_user}", "gists_url": "https://api.github.com/users/kirktrue/gists{/gist_id}", "starred_url": "https://api.github.com/users/kirktrue/starred{/owner}{/repo}", "subscriptions_url": "https://api.github.com/users/kirktrue/subscriptions", "organizations_url": "https://api.github.com/users/kirktrue/orgs", "repos_url": "https://api.github.com/users/kirktrue/repos", "events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/kirktrue/events{/privacy}", "received_events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/kirktrue/received_events", "type": "User", "user_view_type": "public", "site_admin": false}, "body": "Three changes to the `AsyncKafkaConsumer`’s internals to reduce the CPU usage:\r\n\r\n1. Switching from using `Selector.wakeup()` to `Queue.poll()` as the mechanism to alert the network thread that there's work to do (KAFKA-19296)\r\n2. Unrolling the Java Streams API usage into old-style `for` loops to remove overhead in critical path (KAFKA-19297)\r\n3. Removing the random ID generation for each application and background event (KAFKA-19295)", "labels": [{"id": 851033232, "node_id": "MDU6TGFiZWw4NTEwMzMyMzI=", "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/apache/kafka/labels/consumer", "name": "consumer", "color": "bf6a03", "default": false, "description": "", "archived_at": null, "archived_by": null}, {"id": 6979675393, "node_id": "LA_kwDOACG9q88AAAA